          "field": "reason",
          "before": "The old graphical-determination defect is resolved. I read all four actual scaled PNGs and both language versions of the complete main and fresh tasks, models and scoring. Main A tangent points (0;0.72) and (30;0.54) give -0.0060 mol/(L s); secant (0;0.80) to (20;0.60) gives -0.0100. Normalize by coefficient 2. Fresh amount slope -0.0120 mol/s divided by 2 L preserves the concentration rate. Main gas tangent (0;9) to (120;39) gives 0.25 mL/s, compared with secants 0.40 and 0.20; fresh tangent (0;2) to (50;26) gives 0.48 mL/s. Conversion by 24 L/mol and solution volume is correct. Tolerances are realistic and propagated; numbers without graphical derivation do not suffice. Provided diagrams assess evaluation, not experimental recording or graph construction.",
          "current": "Four relationship statements cover secant, tangent, signs/stoichiometry and amount/concentration/gas conversions. New variation axis removes the leaked numerical slope and aligns with whole actual graph-based tasks. No recording/experiment operator is claimed. Bound to sealed FIRST curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-16/chemie-native15-five-whole-P-findings-targeted-author-successor-20261016-v1/P5.complete-whole-profile-author-successors.json; exact after-profile fingerprint pinned in FIRST.science.five-whole-P-successors.record.json. This is technical serialization of that same scientific decision, not another independent review. E/G describes only the identified public authored artifact/design, never actual learner performance or a performed experiment."
        },
