            "reviewedAt": "2026-10-16T20:17:29.536920+00:00",
            "reviewer": "codex-independent-a-equilibrium-polarity-current-context",
            "reason": "Whole eb753 already provides dispersion, permanent dipoles, donor/acceptor hydrogen-bond logic, ion-dipole distinction and the limit of universal boiling rankings, with bonding and EPA foundations. This is an appropriate common interaction-model prerequisite for using the model to interpret solubility and boiling trends. Given methanol/ethane structures and straight-chain C6/C2 comparison do not universally require generating or discussing constitutional alkanol isomers. No complete alcohol nomenclature/oxidation route is removed from its own valid target duties. KEEP unchanged two complete DE/EN application briefs. Methanol32 versus ethane30g/mol controls mass approximately; OH interactions explain higher cohesion and water affinity. C6 straight-chain alcohol has a greater hydrophobic contribution than C2 despite one OH; qualitative lower solubility does not imply a numerical solubility or exception-free law. Own frozen actual science tmp/chemie-m7-resumed-20261016/equilibrium-polarity-two-prior-independent-a-v1/FIRST.two-current-prior-interfaces-and-whole-P-fit.independent-a.science.frozen.json sha256:dad2051c32af429fef7eef4d4ff5b93b7c75492dad0527045c3739549b1bd8c8. Whole profile, material cases, rubric and distinct original criteria retained exactly; this is genuine independent current acquisition-context science with a fresh own identity/date, not a historical reviewer rebind or a new source-union approval. BB/BE GK acquisition HOLD and unchanged source/operator/actual-execution boundaries remain separate and unclosed; no formalD/V or human/learner acceptance.",
