          "before": "Whole original author/historical scientific profile preserved; current review-candidate binding only. Actual independent content/source/native-page approvals remain separate.",
          "current": "Read both complete bilingual cases. Products balance atoms. Protonated carbonyl, tetrahedral intermediate, proton transfer, water departure and regenerated acid are correct for the ester model. The amide cases explicitly require activating dehydration; the cold ammonium salt is not treated as an amide and NH4+ is not called a nucleophile. Methanol/ethylamine changes test O-to-N mechanistic transfer. Current independently inspected native page, source/prerequisite context and materials support this unchanged complete profile. Frozen first judgment: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-16/chemie-native9-current437-fresh-independent-a-20261016-v1/FIRST.independent-current-nine-science-and-separate699.frozen.json sha256:dbdbefe4b37fa1dc2d314b647d1a275d81715783a9c2b6c76ef17ce846d97d4a"
