            "reviewer": "Codex independent P reviewer B after own native-validated frozen D-B; informed author-candidate semantic review; AI candidate only",
            "reason": "INDEPENDENT SEMANTIC PASS / KEEP exact inner profile. Molten NaCl yields the given Na/Cl2 products with matching two-electron half-reaction sums and molar ratio2:1; aqueous CuCl2 with specified inert electrodes and observed Cu/Cl2 gives1:1. Both conserve atoms/charge. The water/competing-electrode limitation is explicit, so no universal aqueous product rule is claimed. Cation/anion transport is distinguished from external electron current; galvanic/electrolysis energy directions are correct. The second case is independent of the molten-salt visualization and changes medium, species, ion charge and ratio. Products/conditions are supplied hypothetical observations, not evidence of a real trial; chlorine/melt experiments are not assigned as personal activities. Scope is supported by HE E.1 and GK/LK Q3.3, without importing Faraday, equilibrium or overpotential requirements. DE/EN agree. AI candidate, needs_human_review, E1/G1; no human approval.",
